Recursive debugging.

    bocl> (quit)


    Debugger invoked on condition of type SIMPLE-ERROR:
      In evale: ERROR: Undefined function: QUIT

    Backtrace (innermost frame first):
       0: (LAMBDA COMMON-LISP::C)
       1: HANDLER-BIND
       2: restart ABORT
       3: BLOCK COMMON-LISP::DONE
       4: (COMMON-LISP::%REPL-EVAL COMMON-LISP::FORM)
       5: CATCH BOCL::%QUIT-CATCH-TAG

    Available restarts:
       0: [ABORT]

Normal error handling so far.

    debug> (boc:quit) 

    In scan_symbol:
    ERROR: READ: there is no package named BOC

    ~/src/public/bocl/issues/open
    master
    13:51[pjb@thalassa org.xquartz:0 open 17Gi]$ echo $?
    65

The debugger must handle errors and call INVOKE-DEBUGGER recursively.
We cannot exit just for a small error (only crash would justify it).
